# Scope and disposition

Read the prior `18-sendmessage-eof-disposition.txt` first. The block was already present in the initial
2026-06-23 repository commit a4736e5; June 25 rebrand retained it. No recorded technical rationale
was found in those source revisions. Therefore this journal does not claim to know the original reason.
Current source has generic schema-driven client tools; provider capability `blocks_default_tools` is not
proof of a SendMessage-specific incompatibility.

# Change

Remove **only `SendMessage`** from DEFAULT_BLOCKED_TOOLS_NON_ANTHROPIC. Keep SendMessageTool,
TeamCreate/TeamDelete/TeammateTool, worktree, schedule, server web and notification defaults unchanged.
Existing explicit providers.<name>.blocked_tools lists/false still override defaults; no user config migration.
Expose this existing setting as **LLM options → Tool blocklist (routed)**, with a JSON list replacement,
false/[] (disable all compatibility blocks), or default/unset/auto reset. Invalid types/JSON do not save.
Tool permission checks are still the CLI's responsibility; native/direct requests bypass router filtering.
The warning explicitly says false/[] includes unsupported server tools. No blanket unblock.

# Runtime evidence

[evidence/verification.json](evidence/verification.json) contains per-run verdicts and final source digests.
Claude CLI version 2.1.310. Every provider response was generated by the owned loopback fixture;
these runs prove CLI execution and router transport, not remote model/tool selection quality.

- Before code change, `run-cielairouter-default-233540`: SendMessage absent, baseline reply succeeds.
- Narrow per-provider allow override, `run-cielairouter-override-233651`: actual Agent tool spawns a
  background child; actual SendMessage tool returns success; child's next upstream request contains
  `OWNED-DELIVERY-721`; child returns `OWNED-CHILD-ACK-721`; parent receives native task notification.
- `run-vllm-override-233753`: same native delivery through OpenAI Chat conversion (`/v1/chat/completions`).
- After default change, **without override**, `run-cielairouter-default-234143` and
  `run-vllm-default-234743`: both child receipt and ACK pass, exit 0.
- Earlier `run-cielairouter-override-233555` returned send success but child stopped before a tool boundary;
  no recipient request with marker was recorded. This is NOT counted as successful delivery proof.

All runs used temporary HOME/config/workspace under C:/Windows/Temp, scrubbed inherited runtime and
provider credentials, dummy key, loopback upstream, blocked proxy egress, exact spawned process-tree
teardown. No live host/config/credential changes, install, commit or push.

# UI and focused checks

Actual portable prelaunch menu opened in an owned Windows console. Navigated to Tool blocklist,
entered ["SendMessage"], verified scoped config file, reset to default and verified key absent.
[evidence/menu/tool-blocklist.png](evidence/menu/tool-blocklist.png) and
[evidence/menu/tool-blocklist-saved.png](evidence/menu/tool-blocklist-saved.png) are PrintWindow captures
of only that owned console. Text captures and roundtrip.json are alongside them.

25 focused tests pass (policy, panel, Cron and review passthrough); inherited CIEL_RUNTIME_* scrubbed,
fresh isolated config and free port before runtime import. Focused Ruff and git diff --check pass.
Strict OKF checker initially hit a Windows stdout encoding error; rerun with -X utf8 passes.
Initial direct unittest invocations failed import resolution under -I; corrected owned focused.py adds
only the chosen repository root before discovery. No full test groups ran.

# Limits

Not verified: old SendMessageTool schema, team lifecycle tools, remote cross-session messages,
real remote provider schema acceptance/model quality, or every upstream protocol. Those claims remain
unknown. Subagent delivery at a tool boundary is verified, not fabricated native agent-team creation.
Work mode/context queue changes are owned by other agents and are not modified by this task.

